cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Aether in research, please cite this repository and the version or commit you evaluated."
title: "Aether: a model-led execution runtime for autonomous computer work"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mohamud"
    given-names: "Mohamud"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamud1961/Aether"
url: "https://github.com/mohamud1961/Aether"
abstract: >-
  Aether is a public research agent runtime investigating whether improvements
  in model intelligence can translate more directly into improvements in
  real-world agent capability without adding a second strategic intelligence
  around the model. The model owns cognition and strategy; Aether supplies
  bounded execution, tools, state, recovery, evidence, and independent
  completion review.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-runtime
  - autonomous-agents
  - evaluation
  - model-agency
  - reproducibility
